9/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e9f67c493312b68153ed88582d196e9a43e9bc68dac7e9916cc5e5587c696eb" "basis" 1144 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/assets/da61a7fd99ce683be4e66d3708ddf15c969b038f0250dc4c024ace870c3f7544.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e9f67c493312b68153ed88582d196e9a43e9bc68dac7e9916cc5e5587c696eb" "basis" 1144 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/assets/ed8a2354f8cc04f998875f599a52b50e6c64cafe8976f1bea176772543e295ac.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e9f67c493312b68153ed88582d196e9a43e9bc68dac7e9916cc5e5587c696eb" "basis" 1144 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/add078cb1b05f772f25c91a4736f5aacd4490ff8556ce6a0d0ea7ad44869d0e7.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/state.json" "file_sha256" "19e86b9b7b125b99f4e259bde169ea1426bc73951562843fcabb437b348f8e72" "basis" 1928 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 10 & 0 & -20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,10)$, $(0,0),$ $(4,-20).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/8c86cb108725b3f1c7b5731dda0f11a5cb21a7daa023c5153cce1ece3ba6ba0f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/state.json" "file_sha256" "19e86b9b7b125b99f4e259bde169ea1426bc73951562843fcabb437b348f8e72" "basis" 1928 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6293cc96a6d4aa4d9688bc8a6add7d10e203b0bfe03b78c08ef4c2c0c4a8f0f8" "basis" 1928 "verific